# The one-fraction adder (folklore; the standard first FRACTRAN example).
# Registers are prime exponents: n = 2^a * 3^b holds a in register 2 and
# b in register 3. Each step moves one unit from register 2 to register 3,
# so the program halts at 3^(a+b).
# Run: lake exe fractran --n 1944 --out final adder.ft   (2^3 * 3^5 -> 3^8 = 6561)

3/2
